WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.340 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  this woman is space spraying she is  applying a mist of insecticide that will  kill the flies and mosquitoes that it  contacts it is immediately effective but  it offers only temporary control other  flies and mosquitoes will enter the  house and the operation must be repeated  this too is space praying but on a  larger scale and out of doors here the  insecticide may be applied in either of  two forms as a mist of tiny droplets  that drift slowly downward or as a fog a  blanketing cloud that swirls through  shrubbery and between houses  in considering outdoor space spraying it  is important to realize that the  majority of flies and mosquitoes remain  within 25 feet of the ground this might  be termed the insect zone and it is this  region that must be treated to achieve  maximum killed mist applicators are  simple in their principle of operation a  fan forces a high velocity blast of air  past the nozzles the insecticide is  injected into this air blast which  breaks the liquid into fine droplets and  projects them out as a mist there are  several types of mist applicators  available some of which project to fine  aerosol spraying most of the larger  machines can be rotated in a full circle  also the nozzle can be directed from  side to side here mist is being  projected directly at fly attractants in  an alley where there are no alleys the  mist is directed in a high arc over the  houses to drift slowly down through the  insects own the speed of this downward  drift is important and is governed by  the size of the droplets if they are  large the mist will fall too rapidly a  fast rate of fall shortens the arc and  cuts down on the width of the swath  cover droplets of the proper size will  carry farther producing a wide swath and  will continue to drift downward in spite  of thermals or rising currents of warm  air on this machines droplet size is  regulated by the velocity of the air  blast the choice of nozzles and the  weight of oil use heavier oil producing  coarser droplets with fog fine droplet  size is desirable as with mist machines  several types of fog generators are  available  most of them operated from trucks  although some types are affordable  the typical thermal generator will  illustrate the principle of operation in  this machine air and gasoline are pumped  into a combustion chamber and ignited  the expanding hot gases pass through the  fog head at terrific velocity the  insecticide is introduced into the  stream of gas and is atomized into fog  contrary to the application of mist fog  is directed along the ground where it  swirls around buildings blanketing the  insect is all since fog is composed of  exceedingly fine droplets it is easily  affected by thermals and light breezes  which will quickly carry it out of the  effective area for this reason fog  should be applied at night or in early  morning or evening when the air is quiet  to measure the effectiveness of space  spray treatment it is important first to  make an appraisal of the fly population  by the grille method or of the mosquito  population by trapping continued routine  sampling during the spray program will  indicate the effectiveness of the  treatment for most effective application  the equipment should travel at about 5  miles per hour and mist directed  downwind with proper droplet size this  will produce a suave 100 feet or more in  will care must be exercised in treating  residential districts oil mist may burn  foliage and spot automobiles therefore  fog is frequently used in neighborhoods  having expensive landscaping but  remember fog is quickly carried away by  light winds and thermals which occur  during the warm part of the day  for best results bomb should be applied  during the still hours of night evening  or early morning but for photographic  purposes we are demonstrating fogging  technique by daylight in this film  commonly the city block is considered  the unit of urban space spray  however if costly insecticides must be  used then treatment of the entire block  on a citywide basis becomes too  expensive under these circumstances spot  spraying may be employed after an insect  concentration is located spray is apply  to this limited area only whether it be  a half block or a single backyard  mist machines can be used effectively  for mosquito larvae sighting directing  the mist downwind so it will carry a  sufficient distance producing a film of  lava Seidel oil on the water surface  airplane space spraying is frequently  employed for wide inaccessible areas  although airplane application is very  expensive and should be done in the  early morning or late evening hour  commercial indoor equipment is available  for use in restaurants but all food and  dishes must be covered before spraying  is begun it must be emphasized that  space spraying depends on contact and  has little or no residual effect partly  this is due to insufficient dosage as  the following demonstration will show  here mist is being applied at a normal  rate the fall of mist is picked up on a  plate of glass this operator is applying  residual insecticide to another glass  plate when both plates dry a comparison  will show the difference the dosage of  the mist is entirely inadequate for  residual effect space spraying then  depends on contact to kill insects the  effect is immediate and it is useful to  gain quick relief from flies and  mosquitoes outdoors effective kill  depends on treating the insects all  within 25 feet of the ground this may be  accomplished by applying a mist of  insecticide that drifts slowly down  through the zone or a fog that blankets  the zone and lingers close to the ground  space spraying is not a cure-all for fly  or mosquito problems it has its use for  quick relief but the results are only  temporary  however used intelligently and in  conjunction with good sanitation  practices space spraying is a useful  tool in any fly control program  [Music]

